`Devi attesting`                                MEANS `an attesting witness` `the WA Devi`    TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`Chandra attesting out of the testator’s sight` MEANS `an attesting witness` `the WA Chandra` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`Bala attesting, incompetent for a reason outside sections 10(2), 11 and 12` MEANS `an attesting witness` `the WA Bala` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`Devi attesting and taking a legacy`            MEANS `an attesting witness` `the WA Devi`    TRUE  FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE
`Bala attesting, his wife taking a legacy`      MEANS `an attesting witness` `the WA Bala`    TRUE  FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE
`Bala attesting as a creditor whose debt is charged` MEANS `an attesting witness` `the WA Bala` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- The same creditor, but he also takes a beneficial legacy under the will, so
-- s 10(1)'s witness limb is made out of him. Built for ROUND 2, R8: without it,
-- nothing on the file could reach the third conjunct of `s 10(1) — the
-- disposition is utterly null and void` on a charge, so the express exception
-- for "charges and directions for the payment of any debt" was never what
-- decided the answer.
`Bala attesting, taking a legacy and a charge for his debt` MEANS `an attesting witness` `the WA Bala` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE

`a pecuniary legacy of $10,000 to Devi`  MEANS `a gift` `the WA Devi`   `a pecuniary legacy`                       10_000  TRUE  TRUE
`a specific devise to Ismail`            MEANS `a gift` `the WA Ismail` `a specific devise or bequest`             100_000 TRUE  TRUE
`a specific devise to Ismail, determinable at his death` MEANS `a gift` `the WA Ismail` `a specific devise or bequest` 100_000 TRUE FALSE
-- A CHARGE IS BENEFICIAL, AND THE EXCEPTION IS WHAT TAKES IT OUT OF s 10(1)
-- (REPAIR, ROUND 2, R8). This fixture used to record the charge as NOT
-- beneficial, which quietly did the exception's work twice over: a charge
-- securing a real debt plainly benefits the creditor, and s 10(1)'s own words
-- treat charges as a class carved OUT of the beneficial gifts it avoids —
-- "any beneficial devise, legacy, estate, interest, gift or appointment ...,
-- other than and except charges and directions for the payment of any debt".
-- Recording it as non-beneficial made the carve-out untestable.
`a charge on the estate for a debt owed to Bala` MEANS `a gift` `the WA Bala` `a charge or direction for the payment of a debt` 5_000 TRUE  FALSE
`a pecuniary legacy of $10,000 to Chandra` MEANS `a gift` `the WA Chandra` `a pecuniary legacy`                    10_000  TRUE  TRUE
`a pecuniary legacy of $10,000 to Bala`  MEANS `a gift` `the WA Bala`   `a pecuniary legacy`                       10_000  TRUE  TRUE
-- A devise to an attesting witness that he does NOT take beneficially — a
-- devise upon trust for somebody else. s 10(1) avoids only a "beneficial"
-- devise, legacy, estate, interest, gift or appointment, so this one stands
-- even though the donee attested and takes elsewhere under the same will.
-- (ROUND 2, R8: the `beneficial` conjunct had no fixture that turned on it.)
`a devise to Bala upon trust, not beneficially` MEANS `a gift` `the WA Bala` `a specific devise or bequest` 50_000 FALSE TRUE
-- The donee of this devise is named by a reference that TWO of the testator's
-- descendants carry. See `the WA Zainab` above: it is a malformed file by design.
`a specific devise to the reference Yasmin and Zainab share` MEANS `a gift` `the WA Zainab` `a specific devise or bequest` 100_000 TRUE TRUE

