-- THE SAME WILL, APPOINTING A GUARDIAN OF SOMEBODY ELSE'S CHILD (CROSS-MODULE
-- ROUND, X1). Suri is not Farid's child, so this is an appointment s 27(3) does
-- not reach — and it is the ONLY conjunct it fails: the privilege holds, the old
-- form is made out, and Farid died in 2023. Before the repair this will and the
-- one above got the same answer.
`the will of Farid, appointing a guardian of a child who is not his` MEANS
    `a will` `the WA Farid` (JUST (YMD 2023 2 2)) FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY EMPTY
             (LIST (`a guardian appointed by the father by will` `the WA Chandra` "suri"))
             FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE

-- TWO APPOINTMENTS IN ONE WILL, one of Farid's own child and one of a stranger's,
-- so that s 27(3)'s distributive reading has something to be distributive over:
-- the list-valued decision must keep the first and drop the second, which no
-- case-level boolean can express. (CROSS-MODULE ROUND, X1.)
`the will of Farid, appointing two guardians, one of them of a child who is not his` MEANS
    `a will` `the WA Farid` (JUST (YMD 2023 2 2)) FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY EMPTY
             (LIST `the guardian Farid appointed of his child Jaya`,
                   (`a guardian appointed by the father by will` `the WA Chandra` "suri"))
             FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE

-- The same informal soldier's will, but Osman died ON 29 August 1938. The
-- appointment is of Osman's own child Suri and not of Farid's child Jaya, so
-- that the ONLY conjunct of s 27(3) this case fails is the commencement — which
-- is what the Osman/Wahid pair is for. (CROSS-MODULE ROUND, X1.)
`the will of Osman` MEANS
    `a will` `the WA Osman` (JUST (YMD 1938 8 1)) FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY EMPTY
             (LIST (`a guardian appointed by the father by will` `the WA Bala` "suri"))
             FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE

-- Kamala's will, executed abroad, but attributed to Nirmala, whose date of
-- death is not in evidence: the s 5 route cannot be opened or closed.
`the will of Nirmala, executed abroad` MEANS
    `a will` `the WA Nirmala` (JUST (YMD 2015 3 1)) TRUE FALSE FALSE EMPTY EMPTY
             EMPTY FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE

-- Rahim's two wills, one on each side of 29 August 1938, each expressed to be
-- made in contemplation of his marriage to Gita.
`the will of Rahim, made on 28 August 1938 in contemplation of his marriage to Gita` MEANS
    `a will` `the WA Rahim` (JUST (YMD 1938 8 28)) TRUE TRUE TRUE
             (LIST `Bala attesting`, `Chandra attesting`)
             EMPTY EMPTY TRUE (JUST "gita") FALSE FALSE

`the will of Rahim, made on 29 August 1938 in contemplation of his marriage to Gita` MEANS
    `a will` `the WA Rahim` (JUST (YMD 1938 8 29)) TRUE TRUE TRUE
             (LIST `Bala attesting`, `Chandra attesting`)
             EMPTY EMPTY TRUE (JUST "gita") FALSE FALSE

-- s 6(2)'s SECOND LIMB, ON ITS OWN (ROUND 2, R4). In writing, signed at the
-- foot, and both witnesses subscribed in her presence — but the signature was
-- never "made or acknowledged by the testator as the signature to his will or
-- codicil in the presence of 2 or more witnesses present at the same time".
-- The only fixture that used to falsify that limb was the will executed
-- abroad, which fails all three limbs at once and has no witnesses at all, so
-- the limb could be deleted with every assertion still green.
`the will of Amrita, the signature never acknowledged before the witnesses` MEANS
    `a will` `the WA Amrita` (JUST (YMD 2015 3 1)) TRUE TRUE FALSE
             (LIST `Bala attesting`, `Chandra attesting`)
             (LIST `a specific devise to Ismail`)
             EMPTY FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE

-- s 12's ANTECEDENT, WHICH NOTHING COULD REACH BEFORE (ROUND 2, R6). Bala both
-- attests the will and is appointed executor by it, so
-- `the attesting witness is an executor appointed by the will` is TRUE of him
-- and s 12's denial can be seen to deny.
`the will of Amrita, Bala being both an executor and an attesting witness` MEANS
    `a will, in full` `the WA Amrita` (JUST (YMD 2015 3 1)) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
                      (LIST `Bala attesting`, `Chandra attesting`)
                      (LIST `a specific devise to Ismail`)
                      EMPTY FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE
                      TRUE (LIST (`an executor appointed by the will` `the WA Bala`))

-- s 6(3)'s EVIDENTIAL CONJUNCT, ON ITS OWN (ROUND 2, R7). The same will as
-- `the will of Amrita, not signed at the foot or end`, except that it is NOT
-- apparent on the face of it that the testator intended to give effect by her
-- signature to the writing signed as her will. Place that signature beside the
-- end and s 6(3)'s positional half is satisfied, so the evidential half is the
-- only thing left to decide it.
`the will of Amrita, not signed at the foot or end, the intention not apparent` MEANS
    `a will, in full` `the WA Amrita` (JUST (YMD 2015 3 1)) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
                      (LIST `Bala attesting`, `Chandra attesting`)
                      (LIST `a specific devise to Ismail`)
                      EMPTY FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE
                      FALSE EMPTY

-- s 10(1)'s TWO UNTESTED CONJUNCTS, IN ONE WILL (ROUND 2, R8). Bala attests,
-- and takes three things: a pecuniary legacy (beneficial, and not a charge —
-- so s 10(1) avoids it), a charge on the estate for a debt owed to him
-- (beneficial, but expressly excepted — so it stands), and a devise he holds
-- upon trust (not a charge, but not beneficial — so it stands too). Because he
-- takes the legacy, s 10(1)'s witness limb is TRUE of him for all three, and
-- each of the other two conjuncts is left alone to decide its own disposition.
`the will of Amrita, whose attesting creditor takes a legacy, a charge and a devise on trust` MEANS
    `a will` `the WA Amrita` (JUST (YMD 2015 3 1)) TRUE TRUE TRUE
             (LIST `Bala attesting, taking a legacy and a charge for his debt`, `Chandra attesting`)
             (LIST `a pecuniary legacy of $10,000 to Bala`,
                   `a charge on the estate for a debt owed to Bala`,
                   `a devise to Bala upon trust, not beneficially`)
             EMPTY FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE

-- s 10(3)'s COUNT AND ITS SUBSCRIPTION FILTER (ROUND 2, R5). Three witnesses,
-- one of whom takes; of the other two, one subscribed out of the testator's
-- sight. Strike the interested witness out and only ONE disinterested
-- subscribing witness remains, so s 10(3) cannot save the legacy — while the
-- will itself is still duly executed, two of the three having subscribed in her
-- presence.
`the will of Amrita, a legacy to one of her three witnesses, another subscribing out of her sight` MEANS
    `a will` `the WA Amrita` (JUST (YMD 2015 3 1)) TRUE TRUE TRUE
             (LIST `Devi attesting and taking a legacy`, `Bala attesting`, `Chandra attesting out of the testator’s sight`)
             (LIST `a pecuniary legacy of $10,000 to Devi`)
             EMPTY FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE

-- s 6(2)'s FIRST LIMB, BY THE HAND OF ANOTHER (ROUND 2). Amrita did not sign;
-- somebody else signed at the foot or end in her presence and by her direction,
-- which is the second alternative s 6(2) allows and which no fixture used to
-- exercise. Everything else is as in the base will, so the will is validly
-- executed.
`the will of Amrita, signed at the foot for her by another at her direction` MEANS
    `a will, in full` `the WA Amrita` (JUST (YMD 2015 3 1)) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
                      (LIST `Bala attesting`, `Chandra attesting`)
                      (LIST `a specific devise to Ismail`)
                      EMPTY FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE
                      TRUE EMPTY

-- THE AMANUENSIS LIMB, LEFT ALONE TO DECIDE (ROUND 2). The same will as above,
-- but it is NOT apparent on the face of it that the testator intended to give
-- effect by that signature — which closes the s 6(3) route and leaves s 6(2)'s
-- first limb resting on the amanuensis alternative alone. It has to be closed,
-- because "signed at the foot or end thereof by some other person in his
-- presence and by his direction" entails a signature placed at the end, so on
-- the will above the deeming holds as well and the two routes cannot be told
-- apart. Nothing here is strained: a signature actually at the foot needs no
-- s 6(3) deeming, which exists for signatures that are not there.
`the will of Amrita, signed at the foot for her by another, the intention not apparent on its face` MEANS
    `a will, in full` `the WA Amrita` (JUST (YMD 2015 3 1)) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
                      (LIST `Bala attesting`, `Chandra attesting`)
                      (LIST `a specific devise to Ismail`)
                      EMPTY FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE
                      FALSE EMPTY

-- s 13(1)'s EXCEPTION HAS TWO LIMBS, AND THIS WILL MAKES OUT ONLY THE FIRST
-- (ROUND 2). It is made in exercise of a power of appointment, but the appointed
-- estate WOULD in default of the appointment pass to the takers s 13(1) names —
-- so on AMBIGUITY A4's reading, which treats "when" as a further condition, the
-- exception does not save it and the marriage revokes it. Nothing used to
-- separate the two limbs: the only appointing fixture made both out at once.
`the will of Amrita, made in exercise of a power, the appointed estate passing in default` MEANS
    `a will` `the WA Amrita` (JUST (YMD 2015 3 1)) TRUE TRUE TRUE
             (LIST `Bala attesting`, `Chandra attesting`)
             (LIST `a specific devise to Ismail`)
             EMPTY FALSE NOTHING TRUE FALSE

-- s 13(2) ASKS TWO THINGS, AND THIS WILL ANSWERS ONLY THE SECOND (ROUND 2). It
-- names Gita as the person the testator was to marry, but it is NOT "expressed
-- to be made in contemplation of a marriage" — which is the distinction the
-- subsection turns on, and which nothing used to test, the two facts having been
-- set together on every fixture. Naming a fiancee is not expressing the will to
-- be made in contemplation of the marriage.
`the will of Amrita, naming Gita but not expressed to be made in contemplation of the marriage` MEANS
    `a will` `the WA Amrita` (JUST (YMD 2015 3 1)) TRUE TRUE TRUE
             (LIST `Bala attesting`, `Chandra attesting`)
             (LIST `a specific devise to Ismail`)
             EMPTY FALSE (JUST "gita") FALSE FALSE

-- s 27(3)'s LAST CONJUNCT, ON ITS OWN (ROUND 2, R9). Farid's will in every
-- particular except that it appoints nobody as guardian: the privilege holds,
-- the death is after 29 August 1938, and there is simply no appointment for
-- s 27(3) to make good.
`the will of Farid, appointing no guardian` MEANS
    `a will` `the WA Farid` (JUST (YMD 2023 2 2)) FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY EMPTY
             EMPTY FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE

GIVEN `the maker of the will` IS A Person
GIVETH A Will
-- A will like Amrita's, made by whoever is named: in writing, signed at the
-- foot, acknowledged before Bala and Chandra, both of whom subscribed. Used by
-- the commencement-boundary cases below, where the will is not what is under
-- test and only the testator's date of death is.
`an ordinary will made by` `the maker of the will` MEANS
    `a will` `the maker of the will` (JUST (YMD 1985 3 1)) TRUE TRUE TRUE
             (LIST `Devi attesting and taking a legacy`, `Bala attesting`, `Chandra attesting`)
             (LIST `a pecuniary legacy of $10,000 to Devi`)
             EMPTY FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE

-- The s 26 soundness case, and see the note on Aisha, Yasmin and Zainab: this
-- is a MALFORMED file, kept only to pin a property of the rule.
`the will of Zubaida, devising to the reference two of her children share` MEANS
    `a will` `the WA Zubaida` (JUST (YMD 2015 3 1)) TRUE TRUE TRUE
             (LIST `Bala attesting`, `Chandra attesting`)
             (LIST `a specific devise to the reference Yasmin and Zainab share`)
             EMPTY FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE

GIVEN
    `the person who died`        IS A Person
    `the family of the deceased` IS A Family
    `the instrument`             IS A Will
GIVETH A `A case under this Act`
-- A case in which nothing has happened except the making of the will: no
-- foreign law, no revocation, no revival, no subsequent conveyance, no
-- contrary intention, no privilege, no application to rectify and no grant.
`a plain case` MEANS
    `a case` (`a WA deceased person` `the person who died` `the family of the deceased` (JUST `the instrument`) EMPTY)
             (`the plain facts about` `the instrument`)
             FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE

GIVEN
    `the person who died`            IS A Person
    `the family of the deceased`     IS A Family
    `the will and its further facts` IS A `A will, with the facts about it that only this Act asks`
    `the grants`                     IS A LIST OF Grant
GIVETH A `A case under this Act`
`a case with` MEANS
    `a case` (`a WA deceased person` `the person who died` `the family of the deceased`
                                  (JUST (`the will and its further facts`'s `the will`)) `the grants`)
             `the will and its further facts`
             FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE


§§ `Worked facts — the alterations, the signature positions and the grants`

GIVEN
    `the earlier words are apparent`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is executed in the like manner`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed in the margin`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed opposite a memorandum`       IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An alteration made in a will after its execution`
`an alteration` MEANS `An alteration made in a will after its execution` WITH
    `the words or effect of the will before the alteration are apparent` IS `the earlier words are apparent`
    `the alteration is executed in the like manner as by this Act is required for the execution of the will` IS `it is executed in the like manner`
    `the signature of the testator and the subscription of the witnesses are made in the margin or on some other part of the will opposite or near to the alteration` IS `signed in the margin`
    `the signature of the testator and the subscription of the witnesses are made at the foot or end of or opposite to a memorandum referring to the alteration and written at the end or some other part of the will` IS `signed opposite a memorandum`

`an obliteration that leaves the earlier words legible, unattested`   MEANS `an alteration` TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an obliteration that leaves the earlier words illegible, unattested` MEANS `an alteration` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an interlineation, the earlier words legible, signed in the margin`  MEANS `an alteration` TRUE  FALSE TRUE  FALSE
`an interlineation, the earlier words legible, signed opposite a memorandum` MEANS `an alteration` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Executed in the like manner as the will itself, which is s 16(1)'s own
-- escape and does not need the s 16(2) deeming.
`an interlineation, the earlier words legible, executed in the like manner as the will` MEANS `an alteration` TRUE TRUE  FALSE FALSE

GIVEN `where it stands` IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A disposition, and where it stands in relation to the signature`
-- Three positions, selected by a string so that the three literals below read
-- as three positions of one gift rather than as three gifts.
`the devise to Ismail` MEANS `A disposition, and where it stands in relation to the signature` WITH
    `the disposition`                       IS `a specific devise to Ismail`
    `underneath or following the signature`  IS `where it stands` EQUALS "below the signature"
    `inserted after the signature was made`  IS `where it stands` EQUALS "inserted after the signature was made"

`the grant of probate made on 1 March 2020` MEANS
    `a WA grant` `probate` (JUST (YMD 2020 3 1)) `not limited` FALSE NOTHING
-- A grant made on the last day of a 31-day month, which is where a six-month
-- period computed by carrying the day across used to overshoot: see the note on
-- `six months after`.
`the grant of probate made on 31 August 2020` MEANS
    `a WA grant` `probate` (JUST (YMD 2020 8 31)) `not limited` FALSE NOTHING
-- A grant whose date is not in evidence. It cannot be shown not to have been
-- the first, so it cannot be passed over in favour of a later dated grant.
`a grant of probate whose date is not in evidence` MEANS
    `a WA grant` `probate` NOTHING `not limited` FALSE NOTHING
`the grant limited to settled land made on 1 February 2020` MEANS
    `a WA grant` `letters of administration with the will annexed` (JUST (YMD 2020 2 1)) `limited to settled land or to trust property` FALSE NOTHING
`the grant limited to a part of the estate made on 1 February 2020` MEANS
    `a WA grant` `letters of administration with the will annexed` (JUST (YMD 2020 2 1)) (`limited to a part only of the testator’s estate` "the Malaysian assets") FALSE NOTHING
`the probate resealed on 1 September 2020, granted on 1 March 2020` MEANS
    `a WA grant` `probate` (JUST (YMD 2020 3 1)) `not limited` TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 9 1))
-- A PLAIN GRANT OF LETTERS OF ADMINISTRATION, SEALED. s 28(5) re-dates only "any
-- probate, or letters of administration WITH THE WILL ANNEXED, sealed under
-- section 47(1)" — a plain grant of letters of administration is outside the
-- deeming even though it carries the sealing flag and a sealing date, so its
-- date remains the date of the grant. (ROUND 2, R9: the module's note claimed
-- "the kind is tested and not just the sealing flag" and no fixture tested it.)
`the letters of administration sealed on 1 September 2020, granted on 1 March 2020` MEANS
    `a WA grant` `letters of administration` (JUST (YMD 2020 3 1)) `not limited` TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 9 1))


