-- THE WILL-LEVEL RULES TAKE THE WRAPPER, NOT THE BARE `Will`, because s 6(2)
-- now reads s 6(3), which reads the position of the signature. These are the
-- wrappers the s 6, s 7(2) and s 8 directives are run on.
`the facts about the will of Amrita`                  MEANS `the plain facts about` `the will of Amrita`
`the facts about the will of Amrita, not in writing`  MEANS `the plain facts about` `the will of Amrita, not in writing`
`the facts about the will of Amrita, only one witness having subscribed in her presence` MEANS `the plain facts about` `the will of Amrita, only one witness having subscribed in her presence`
`the facts about the will of Amrita, executed abroad` MEANS `the plain facts about` `the will of Amrita, executed abroad`
`the facts about the will of Amrita, a legacy to one of her three witnesses` MEANS `the plain facts about` `the will of Amrita, a legacy to one of her three witnesses`

GIVEN `the instrument`         IS A Will
      `where the signature is` IS A `The position of the signature`
GIVETH A `A will, with the facts about it that only this Act asks`
-- A will about which nothing has happened except its making, with the position
-- of the signature stated rather than derived. s 6(3) is the only provision
-- that reads it.
`the facts about a will, the signature being placed thus` MEANS
    `the facts about a will, in full` `the instrument` `where the signature is`
                                      `no conformity to any law outside this Act`
                                      `not revoked in any of those ways` `no revival`
                                      FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- Not signed at the foot or end, but signed BESIDE the end: s 6(3) deems the
-- will valid as far as regards the position of the signature, and s 6(2)'s
-- first limb is satisfied by the deeming.
`the facts about the will of Amrita, signed beside the end` MEANS
    `the facts about a will, the signature being placed thus` `the will of Amrita, not signed at the foot or end` `the signature beside the end of the will`
-- The same will, signed at the HEAD, above every dispositive word. The
-- testator's intention is just as apparent on the face of it, but the signature
-- is not "so placed at or after, or following, or under, or beside, or opposite
-- to the end of the will", so the deeming does not reach it.
`the facts about the will of Amrita, signed at the head` MEANS
    `the facts about a will, the signature being placed thus` `the will of Amrita, not signed at the foot or end` `the signature at the head of the will, above all the dispositive words`

`the case of a will signed beside the end rather than at the foot` MEANS
    `a case with` `the WA Amrita` `no marriages` `the facts about the will of Amrita, signed beside the end` EMPTY
`the case of a will signed at the head, above all the dispositive words` MEANS
    `a case with` `the WA Amrita` `no marriages` `the facts about the will of Amrita, signed at the head` EMPTY

-- s 6(3)'s TWO CONJUNCTS AND ITS PRESUPPOSITION, EACH LEFT ALONE TO DECIDE
-- (ROUND 2, R7 and R11). The signature sits beside the end in all three, so the
-- positional conjunct is TRUE throughout and only the other thing varies:
--   the second is the same will with the testator's intention NOT apparent on
--     the face of it, so the evidential conjunct alone defeats the deeming;
--   the third records no signature at all, so the presupposition alone does.
`the facts about the will of Amrita, signed beside the end, the intention not apparent` MEANS
    `the facts about a will, the signature being placed thus` `the will of Amrita, not signed at the foot or end, the intention not apparent` `the signature beside the end of the will`
`the facts about the will of Amrita, the position stated but nobody having signed` MEANS
    `the facts about a will, the signature being placed thus` `the will of Amrita, not signed at the foot or end` `the position stated as beside the end, though nobody signed the will`

`the case of a will signed beside the end, the intention not apparent on its face` MEANS
    `a case with` `the WA Amrita` `no marriages` `the facts about the will of Amrita, signed beside the end, the intention not apparent` EMPTY
`the case of a will nobody signed, the position being stated as beside the end` MEANS
    `a case with` `the WA Amrita` `no marriages` `the facts about the will of Amrita, the position stated but nobody having signed` EMPTY

-- s 6(2)'s SECOND LIMB, LEFT ALONE TO DECIDE (ROUND 2, R4).
`the facts about the will of Amrita, the signature never acknowledged before the witnesses` MEANS
    `the plain facts about` `the will of Amrita, the signature never acknowledged before the witnesses`
`the case of a will whose signature was never acknowledged before the witnesses` MEANS
    `a case with` `the WA Amrita` `no marriages` `the facts about the will of Amrita, the signature never acknowledged before the witnesses` EMPTY

-- s 6(2)'s FIRST LIMB BY THE HAND OF ANOTHER (ROUND 2).
`the facts about the will of Amrita, signed for her by another` MEANS
    `the plain facts about` `the will of Amrita, signed at the foot for her by another at her direction`
`the case of a will signed at the foot for the testator by another at her direction` MEANS
    `a case with` `the WA Amrita` `no marriages` `the facts about the will of Amrita, signed for her by another` EMPTY

`the facts about the will of Amrita, signed for her by another, the intention not apparent` MEANS
    `the plain facts about` `the will of Amrita, signed at the foot for her by another, the intention not apparent on its face`
-- The same will, with s 10(3)'s counterfactual presence limb proved, so that the
-- amanuensis alternative can be isolated there too: both witnesses take nothing
-- and both subscribed, so the count is 2 and only the signing limb is in issue.
`the case of a will signed for the testator by another, the intention not apparent` MEANS
    `a case with` `the WA Amrita` `no marriages`
                  (`the facts about a will` `the will of Amrita, signed at the foot for her by another, the intention not apparent on its face`
                                            `no conformity to any law outside this Act`
                                            `not revoked in any of those ways` `no revival`
                                            TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
                  EMPTY

-- s 10(3)'s COUNTERFACTUAL PRESENCE LIMB, LEFT ALONE TO DECIDE (ROUND 2). The
-- three-witness will, where TWO disinterested witnesses do subscribe in her
-- presence — so the count is made out — but nobody has proved that the signature
-- was made or acknowledged before two or more of them present at the same time
-- counting only the disinterested. No case used to have the count satisfied and
-- the presence limb not, so the presence limb could be deleted with the whole
-- suite still green.
`the case of a legacy to one of three witnesses, the presence limb not being proved` MEANS
    `a plain case` `the WA Amrita` `no marriages` `the will of Amrita, a legacy to one of her three witnesses`

-- s 13's TWO FORKS, EACH LEFT ALONE TO DECIDE (ROUND 2).
`the case of a will made under a power whose appointed estate passes in default, Amrita marrying Gita` MEANS
    `a plain case` `the WA Amrita` `married Gita in 2018, after the will` `the will of Amrita, made in exercise of a power, the appointed estate passing in default`
`the case of a will naming Gita but not expressed to be made in contemplation, Amrita marrying Gita` MEANS
    `a plain case` `the WA Amrita` `married Gita in 2018, after the will` `the will of Amrita, naming Gita but not expressed to be made in contemplation of the marriage`

-- s 12's ANTECEDENT, ON A CASE WHERE IT HOLDS (ROUND 2, R6).
`the facts about the will of Amrita, Bala being both an executor and an attesting witness` MEANS
    `the plain facts about` `the will of Amrita, Bala being both an executor and an attesting witness`

-- s 10(1)'s CHARGE EXCEPTION AND ITS `beneficial` CONJUNCT (ROUND 2, R8).
`the case of a will giving its attesting creditor a legacy, a charge and a devise on trust` MEANS
    `a plain case` `the WA Amrita` `no marriages` `the will of Amrita, whose attesting creditor takes a legacy, a charge and a devise on trust`

-- s 10(3)'s COUNT, LEFT ALONE TO DECIDE (ROUND 2, R5). The two-witness will
-- again, but this time the counterfactual presence limb is PROVED, so the only
-- thing that can defeat `the will is duly executed without the attestation of
-- any such person` is that striking the interested witness out leaves ONE.
