GIVEN `the family of the deceased`               IS A Family
      `the revocation facts`                     IS A `The ways in which a will may have been revoked`
      `the conveyance is itself the revoking act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A case under this Act`
-- Amrita's will, with a conveyance or other act made after it that relates to
-- the estate the will comprises. The last two arguments are what s 18 turns on:
-- how (if at all) the will was revoked, and whether THIS conveyance is the act
-- that revoked it.
`the case of Amrita’s will and a conveyance made after it` MEANS
    `a case with` `the WA Amrita` `the family of the deceased`
                  (`the facts about a will, in full` `the will of Amrita` `the signature in an unremarkable position`
                                                     `no conformity to any law outside this Act`
                                                     `the revocation facts` `no revival`
                                                     FALSE TRUE `the conveyance is itself the revoking act`
                                                     FALSE FALSE FALSE)
                  EMPTY

-- A conveyance, and no revocation of any kind: s 18 protects the will.
`the case of a conveyance made after the will, the will standing` MEANS
    `the case of Amrita’s will and a conveyance made after it` `no marriages` `not revoked in any of those ways` FALSE
-- The conveyance IS the revoking act — a writing declaring an intention to
-- revoke, executed as a will must be. This is the one case s 18 excepts.
`the case of a conveyance that is itself the act by which the will is revoked` MEANS
    `the case of Amrita’s will and a conveyance made after it` `no marriages` (`revoked` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE
-- A conveyance, and a revocation — but by the marriage, which is not an act of
-- or relating to the estate and is not the conveyance. s 18 still protects the
-- will against the conveyance. This is the case the old encoding got backwards.
`the case of a conveyance made after the will, the will having been revoked by a marriage` MEANS
    `the case of Amrita’s will and a conveyance made after it` `married Gita in 2018, after the will` `not revoked in any of those ways` FALSE
-- THE TWO CASES THAT LEAVE EACH NEW CONJUNCT ALONE TO DECIDE (ROUND 2, R3).
-- The repair above added two conjuncts, and the four cases it came with
-- constrained only their conjunction: every one of them made both FALSE
-- together, so either could be deleted with all the assertions still green.
--
--   (i) A conveyance, and a revocation in one of the ways s 15 allows — by
--       another will or codicil, which IS an act of a description s 15(b)
--       names — but this conveyance is not that act. The s 15 limb conjunct is
--       TRUE and only the tie is FALSE.
`the case of a conveyance made after the will, the will having been revoked by a later will` MEANS
    `the case of Amrita’s will and a conveyance made after it` `no marriages` (`revoked` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE
--  (ii) A conveyance said to BE the act by which the will is revoked, but no
--       mode of revocation in s 15 is made out — which is the case s 14 exists
--       for: "No will shall be revoked by any presumption of an intention on
--       the ground of an alteration in circumstances." A party who conveys the
--       subject-matter and says the will fell with it has s 18 and s 14 both
--       against him. The tie conjunct is TRUE and only the s 15 limb is FALSE.
`the case of a conveyance said to be the revoking act, no mode of revocation in section 15 being made out` MEANS
    `the case of Amrita’s will and a conveyance made after it` `no marriages` `not revoked in any of those ways` TRUE

`the case of a will showing a contrary intention as to the time from which it speaks` MEANS
    `a case with` `the WA Amrita` `no marriages`
                  (`the facts about a will` `the will of Amrita` `no conformity to any law outside this Act`
                                            `not revoked in any of those ways` `no revival`
                                            FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
                  EMPTY

`the case of a will showing a contrary intention as to lapse` MEANS
    `a case with` `the WA Amrita` `no marriages`
                  (`the facts about a will` `the will of Amrita` `no conformity to any law outside this Act`
                                            `not revoked in any of those ways` `no revival`
                                            FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
                  EMPTY

